cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or findings, please cite as below."
title: "Score saturation in deep learning regulatory variant prediction"
authors:
  - family-names: "Amrutham"
    given-names: "Kavya"
    affiliation: "Barnard College, Columbia University"
    email: "ka3041@barnard.edu"
date-released: 2026-04-27
url: "https://github.com/kavya1a/regulatory-score-saturation"
abstract: >
  Quantile-normalized AlphaGenome scores collapse to a near-binary signal on
  regulatory-enriched variant sets. We demonstrate this saturation on Tewhey 2016
  MPRA variants and three independent GWAS datasets, and show that raw model
  outputs restore a 5x improvement in correlation with experimental measurements.
keywords:
  - GWAS
  - regulatory genomics
  - variant scoring
  - MPRA
  - AlphaGenome
  - quantile normalization
  - fine-mapping
license: MIT
